00:29:49.510 --> 00:29:51.430
So here's the command
I'm going to use.

00:29:51.430 --> 00:29:54.040
I'll paste it in here.

00:29:54.040 --> 00:29:57.600
Now, minus q option
is telling it how many

00:29:57.600 --> 00:29:58.613
requests per second.

00:29:58.613 --> 00:30:00.030
So I'm going to
drive this traffic

00:30:00.030 --> 00:30:02.790
at 1,000 requests per second.

00:30:02.790 --> 00:30:05.660
Minus C is how many
parallel workers I want.

00:30:05.660 --> 00:30:07.850
So we will have 200 parallel.

00:30:07.850 --> 00:30:08.850
It's not really threads.

00:30:08.850 --> 00:30:12.330
They're go routines
because this program was

00:30:12.330 --> 00:30:14.190
written in the Go language.

00:30:14.190 --> 00:30:19.140
And the minus z tells
how long to run for.

00:30:19.140 --> 00:30:21.810
I'm going to actually
change that to 15 seconds,

00:30:21.810 --> 00:30:23.430
so we're not waiting too long.

00:30:23.430 --> 00:30:26.870
And the last thing I'm going
